# STL String & Vector — Quick Example Reference

Short, runnable snippets for every common operation. Each one is minimal on purpose — copy, run, tweak.

---

## std::string

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
using namespace std;
```

**Declaring**
```cpp
string s1;              // empty string
string s2 = "hello";    // direct init
string s3(5, '*');      // "*****"
```

**Reading input**
```cpp
string name;
cin >> name;            // reads ONE word, stops at space
getline(cin, name);     // reads the whole line, including spaces
```

**Size & access**
```cpp
string s = "hello";
cout << s.size();       // 5
cout << s[0];            // 'h' — no bounds check
cout << s.at(1);          // 'e' — throws if out of range
cout << s.front();       // 'h'
cout << s.back();        // 'o'
```

**Adding to a string**
```cpp
string s = "hi";
s += " there";           // "hi there"
s.append("!");           // "hi there!"
s.push_back('?');        // "hi there!?"
```

**Concatenation**
```cpp
string a = "code", b = "master";
string combined = a + b;  // "codemaster"
```

**Comparison**
```cpp
string a = "apple", b = "banana";
if (a == b) { /* equal */ }
if (a < b)  { /* a comes first alphabetically */ }
```

**Substring**
```cpp
string s = "Learn programming today";
string part = s.substr(6, 11);  // "programming"
//                     ^start  ^length
```

**Searching**
```cpp
string s = "I love coding";
size_t pos = s.find("love");     // 2
if (pos != string::npos)
    cout << "Found at " << pos;
```

**Erase / insert / replace**
```cpp
string s = "Hello World";
s.erase(5, 6);              // "Hello"
s.insert(5, " C++");        // "Hello C++"
s.replace(0, 5, "Hi");      // "Hi C++"
```

**Clear / empty check**
```cpp
s.clear();
if (s.empty()) cout << "empty!";
```

